==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 10~40 seconds<sup>300f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Duche]]s spawn, delay 10~40 seconds<sup>300f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attack Cats]] like [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] in this battle. You should be able to eliminate the Metal Hippoes and Duches quite easily with meatshields and UFO Cat. Spawn Bahamut Cat once you have collected enough money to do so.

When you reach the enemy base and your cats start attacking it, prepare for the 3 Shadow Boxers that will appear; they will tear through your UFOs. Protect Bahamut with stalling cats such as [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall]] and [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho]] so he can attack the Shadow Boxer Ks. If you still can't defeat the Shadow Boxer Ks, consider adding more ranged attackers, namely [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]].

